{"id": "f0af0f49-cec5-4561-9b3e-1505a5e8c40f", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T05:52:21.407113", "source": "user", "parent_id": "406d2089-0332-405b-bf92-e9749b255f91", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Initial inspection request. Please do the following and report back — do NOT write the full design yet, only a brief proposed approach with assumptions and uncertainties. (Note from brief: experimental execution is not required; this is a design-only task, and the runtime has no GPU, so any proposed execution must be acknowledged as a paper-design rather than something to run here. Network is disabled, so you cannot fetch external artifacts live; work from the supplied context and general knowledge. Do not fabricate repository contents or dataset statistics you have not actually inspected. Honest uncertainty is better than invented specifics. Treat the RepoBench paper/scheme — GPT-2 vs CodeLlama-7b on the Python split, cross_file_first — as the target to design around, but flag any detail you are inferring rather than reading. Per submission contract we need: rationale, controls, analysis plan, and feasibility. With that in mind: (1) Quickly inspect /workspace (top-level only is fine) and any local docs (e.g., /workspace/track.md if present) and tell me what is there. (2) Sketch a concise proposed approach covering: research question and hypothesis framing, independent variables (model: GPT-2 family vs CodeLlama-7b/code family), dependent variables (RepoBench Python cross_file_first metric — clarify whether ES/EM/token-level F1, or something else — and call out this as an assumption if not confirmed), dataset subset and sample size / sampling strategy (random, stratified, fixed-seed), prompting setup (zero-shot vs few-shot, exact prompt template, max context length handling, special tokens, code-as-natural-language vs FIM mode — note this is a key assumption you must own), generation config (temperature, top_p, max new tokens, batching), controls/baselines (model size parity considerations, random/majority baseline, copy-the-import baseline if appropriate, optional retrieval of the gold next line for oracle ceiling), evaluation pipeline (exact-match and edit-similarity thresholds, normalization rules, language-aware tokenization, handling of incomplete or out-of-context generations), statistical analysis plan (paired comparison across instances, bootstrap CI on mean accuracy, effect size, multiple-comparisons correction if more than two models are added), and feasibility discussion (compute footprint for a 7B model vs GPT-2 small, dataset size, runtime estimate, what would be cut for a reduced-budget variant). (3) List uncertainties and assumptions you cannot resolve from the supplied context, e.g., which GPT-2 size to pick, which CodeLlama-7b variant, whether 'cross_file_first' refers to the next-line prediction task or the next chunk/identifier task, exact metric definitions, and licensing/environment availability. Keep the report compact and structured; we will iterate on it next turn before you produce the final design document.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does the performance of a small language model (e.g., GPT-2) compare to a larger code-specialized model (e.g., CodeLlama-7b) on the RepoBench Python dataset for the 'cross_file_first' setting?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
