{"id": "15b70c0d-4004-4cc8-82aa-1179460f2e14", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T05:54:14.793752", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "74422905-01c9-4c8e-a452-ed6cb0fb1999", "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "## 1. Inspection findings (evidence)\n\n`/workspace` contains **only** `task.json`. The JSON records the question, the constraint \"Do not claim that an experiment was run\", and an inline note: `track.md` = \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"\n\nVerified observations:\n- `ls -la /workspace` -> single file `task.json` (491 bytes).\n- `inspect_repository /workspace/task.json` -> confirms task structure above.\n- `find / -maxdepth 3 -name track.md` -> no hits outside the JSON reference.\n- `find / -maxdepth 3 -name README*` -> only `/lib/ispell/README.select-ispell` (unrelated system file).\n- `ls -la /` -> writable home is `/workspace` (no `/workspace/datasets`, `/workspace/data`, no README, no source code).\n\nTherefore the deliverable is a **paper design**; no execution is performed or claimed. RepoBench-specific facts I cite are recalled (Bairi et al. 2023, arXiv:2306.03091) and **NOT source-verified here**; flagged.\n\nRepoBench recalled facts (flagged for confirmation):\n- `cross_file_first` = context-ordering variant where cross-file retrieved snippets precede the in-file prefix (paired with `cross_file_last`).\n- Metrics in the original paper: **Edit Similarity (ES, codexglue-style char-level)** as primary, **Exact Match (EM)** as secondary.\n- Splits: random vs hard (retrieval-filtered); next-line granularity is canonical; next-chunk is a separate setting.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Proposed approach (compact)\n\n### 2.1 RQ & hypotheses\n- RQ: Does a small non-code LM (GPT-2 family) match, fall behind, or exceed a 7B code-specialized LM (CodeLlama-7b) on RepoBench Python `cross_file_first` repository-level next-line completion, under matched context and decoding budget?\n- H1: CodeLlama-7b > GPT-2 family on both ES and EM.\n- H0: no difference;