mptions": ["ES is the primary metric and EM is the secondary, both per Bairi et al. 2023 (arXiv:2306.03091). Metric is CodeXGLUE-style character-level edit similarity and exact match.", "cross_file_first denotes the context-ordering variant of cross-file retrieval where cross-file snippets are prepended before the in-file prefix in the prompt.", "GPT-2 Small (124M) is the canonical 'small' model arm; GPT-2 medium is a size-parity sensor only.", "CodeLlama-7b-Python is the appropriate code-specialized 7B variant.", "Mode A (code-as-natural-language concatenation) is the primary paired prompt format applied identically to both arms; Mode B (FIM with PRE/SUF markers) is reported only as a CodeLlama-only arm.", "Per-instance paired test is the primary statistical unit; per-repo median reported as sensitivity, not primary.", "Python dependencies (transformers, torch, datasets, scipy, ES utility) are not preinstalled in this runtime but assumed installable in a real execution environment.", "RepoBench dataset is assumed available as a pre-packaged local copy because the runtime is network-disabled and no artifact was found under /workspace."], "uncertainties": ["Which GPT-2 size variant the brief intends (small/medium/large/XL).", "Which CodeLlama-7b variant (base / Python / Instruct) is meant.", "Exact semantics of cross_file_first in the supplied RepoBench version: context-ordering, split name, or both.", "Primary metric: ES/EM (CodeXGLUE) vs identifier-level F1 vs both.", "Target granularity: next-line, next-chunk, or both.", "Whether the random split or the hard split is the primary endpoint.", "ES tokenization convention: character-level Levenshtein vs token-merge edits.", "Truncation rule when context exceeds model window.", "Whether to include the FIM (Mode B) contrast at all, and only as a CodeLlama-only arm.", "Whether dependency installation and local vendoring of the dataset are in scope for the design document.", "Decoding budget policy: greedy-only vs the proposed 0.0/0.2/0.8 temperature sweep.", "Sample size is reasonable: 1000 primary, 100 reduced-budget."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-607354a7-2b6b-428b-9062-b28d6d66dde4", "tool_call": {"id": "call-607354a7-2b6b-428b-9062-b28d6d66dde4", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Initial inspection + proposed plan\", \"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"## 1. Inspection findings (evidence)\\n\\n`/workspace` contains **only** `task.json`. The JSON records the question, the constraint \\\"Do not claim that an experiment was run\\\", and an inline note: `track.md` = \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"\\n\\nVerified observations:\\n- `ls -la /workspace` -> single file `task.json` (491 bytes).\\n- `inspect_repository /workspace/task.json` -> confirms task structure above.\\n- `find / -maxdepth 3 -name track.md` -> no hits outside the JSON reference.\\n- `find / -maxdepth 3 -name README*` -> only `/lib/ispell/README.select-ispell` (unrelated system file).\\n- `ls -la /` -> writable home is `/workspace` (no `/workspace/datasets`, `/workspace/data`, no README, no source code).\\n\\nTherefore the deliverable is a **paper design**; no execution is performed or claimed. RepoBench-specific facts I cite are recalled (Bairi et al. 2023, arXiv:2306.03091) and **NOT source-verified here**; flagged.\\n\\nRepoBench recalled facts (flagged for confirmation):\\n- `cross_file_first` = context-ordering variant where cross-file retrieved snippets precede the in-file prefix (paired with `cross_file_last`).\\n- Metrics in the original paper: **Edit Similarity (ES, codexglue-style char-level)** as primary, **Exact Match (EM)** as secondary.\\n- Splits: random vs hard (retrieval-filtered); next-line granularity is canonical; next-chunk is a separate setting.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Proposed approach (compact)\\n\\n### 2.1 RQ & hypotheses\\n- RQ: Does a small non-code LM (GPT-2 family) match, fall behind, or exceed a 7B code-specialized LM (CodeLlama-7b) on RepoBench Python `cross_file_first` repository-level next-line completion, under matched context and decoding budget?\\n- H1: CodeLlama-7b > GPT-2 family on both ES and EM.\\n- H0: no difference; reject at alpha=0.05 via paired bootstrap CI on per-instance deltas.\\n\\n### 2.2 Independent variables\\n- Model family: GPT-2 small (124M) primary; GPT-2 medium (355M) as size-parity sensor.\\n- Specialization: CodeLlama-7b-Python primary; CodeLlama-7b base as specialization-ablation.\\n- Prompt mode: code-as-natural-language (both); FIM (`<FILL_ME>`-style markers, CodeLlama-only).\\n- Decoding temperature: 0.0 greedy primary; 0.2 and 0.8 for ES sensitivity only.\\n\\n### 2.3 Dependent variables (confirm metric)\\n- ES (primary): CodeXGLUE-style character-level edit similarity, 0-100.\\n- EM (secondary): binary after whitespace normalization, per-instance.\\n- Identifier-level F1 reported only if confirmed as a standard metric.\\n- Empty / out-of-context / over-generation outputs are scored 0.\\n\\n### 2.4 Dataset & sampling\\n- RepoBench Python `cross_file_first` split; random subset primary, hard subset as sensitivity.\\n- N = 1000 for primary paired analysis; N = 100 for reduced-budget variant.\\n- Sampling: deterministic seed=42, stratified by repository to limit over-representation; paired samples (same prompt -> two models).\\n\\n### 2.5 Prompting (KEY ASSUMPTION)\\n- Mode A (primary, paired): `[system instruction] + [cross-file retrieved snippets with file-path header] + [in-file prefix up to cursor]`; prediction = first emitted line.\\n- Mode B (FIM, CodeLlama-only): PRE/SUF markers per CodeLlama FIM spec; not paired against GPT-2.\\n- Same per-instance truncation rule (`last-min(model_window, max_prompt_tokens)` tokens) applied to both arms to preserve pairing.\\n\\n### 2.6 Generation config\\n- Temperature: 0.0 greedy primary; 0.2 and 0.8 for sensitivity.\\n- top_p: 0.95 (non-greedy only).\\n- max_new_tokens: 128; truncate to predicted single line for EM scoring.\\n- n samples per instance: 1.\\n- Batching: dynamic padding, mini-batch sized to compute budget.\\n\\n### 2.7 Controls / baselines\\n- Majority-class baseline (most-frequent next line in train).\\n- Copy-prefix baseline (echo last in-file non-empty line).\\n- Copy-import baseline (first imported identifier; retrieval-dependence sanity).\\n- Random-token baseline (lower-bound sanity).\\n- Oracle ceiling (gold next line vs itself = 100).\\n- Post-hoc size-parity plot: ES vs log10(params) across GPT-2 small/medium/large/XL where feasible.\\n\\n### 2.8 Evaluation pipeline\\n- Normalization: trim whitespace, collapse repeated spaces; preserve identifiers and string case; do not strip comments unless gold also strips.\\n- ES: character-level Levenshtein per CodeXGLUE convention (flag whether token-merge edits preferred).\\n- EM: exact string match after normalization, binary.\\n- Out-of-context / empty / OOD generations: ES=0, EM=0; counted in denominator.\\n- Per-repo aggregation to detect repository-level clustering effects.\\n\\n### 2.9 Statistical analysis\\n- Primary: paired non-parametric bootstrap (B=10000, seed=42) on per-instance Delta-ES and Delta-EM; percentile CI.\\n- Effect size: Cohen's d (paired) for ES; Cohen's h for EM.\\n- Multi-comparison: Holm-Bonferroni within the model-family family; single primary contrast applies no correction.\\n- Sensitivity: random-vs-hard split, context-length deciles, per-repo median.\\n\\n### 2.10 Feasibility (no-GPU, CPU-only, network off)\\n- GPT-2 small CPU fp32: minutes per 1k instances (tractable).\\n- CodeLlama-7b CPU INT4 (GPTQ/AWQ): ~0.5-2 tok/s/thread -> ~30-60 min on this 24-CPU host.\\n- CodeLlama-7b CPU fp16: infeasible without a GPU.\\n- Python deps (`transformers`, `torch`, `datasets`, `scipy`, ES impl) NOT preinstalled; installable only in a real environment; flagged.\\n- RepoBench dataset not bundled; design assumes pre-packaged local copy under network-disabled mode; flagged.\\n- Reduced-budget variant (recommended): N=100, greedy, INT4 CodeLlama, GPT-2 small only, drop Mode B and temperature sweep -> ~5-10 min in principle. **No execution performed or claimed.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Uncertainties & assumptions requiring your confirmation\\n\\n1. GPT-2 size: small (124M) chosen as canonical; brief silent.\\n2. CodeLlama-7b variant: Python vs base vs Instruct; recommend Python for code-specialized arm.\\n3. `cross_file_first` semantics: context-ordering (cross-file snippets prepended) per my recollection; please verify.\\n4. Primary metric: ES/EM (CodeXGLUE) primary vs Identifier-F1 vs both.\\n5. Target granularity: next-line (default) vs next-chunk.\\n6. Random vs hard split primary endpoint.\\n7. FIM arm: CodeLlama supports `<FILL_ME>` markers; confirm whether to report Mode B (CodeLlama-only).\\n8. ES tokenization: character-level Levenshtein vs token-merge edits.\\n9. Truncation rule: \\\"last-min(model_window, max_prompt_tokens)\\\" tokens, applied identically to both arms.\\n10. Dataset licensing / local packaging: design assumes pre-vendored local copy; off-environment fetch out of scope.\\n11. Identifier-F1 inclusion: report or skip.\\n12. Statistical unit: per-instance paired primary, per-repo sensitivity; confirm.\\n\\n**Awaiting your approval or revisions before producing the full design (stage=result).**\", \"evidence\": \"Only file in /workspace is /workspace/task.json (`ls -la /workspace` returns single 491-byte file; `inspect_repository /workspace/task.json` confirms task structure with public question, context note \\\"Do not claim that an experiment was run\\\", and documents.track.md value \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\"). `find / -maxdepth 3 -name track.md` returns nothing outside the JSON reference. `find / -maxdepth 3 -name README*` returns only /lib/ispell/README.select-ispell (unrelated). Root listing shows /workspace, /home, /tmp, /etc writable; no datasets, no source code, no model artifacts anywhere under /workspace. Recalled RepoBench facts (metric ES+EM per CodeXGLUE, cross_file_first as context-ordering variant, random and hard splits, next-line granularity, Bairi et al. 2023 / arXiv:2306.03091) are background knowledge and explicitly flagged in the answer as not source-verified.\", \"assumptions\": [\"ES is the primary metric and EM is the secondary, both per Bairi et al. 2023 (arXiv:2306.03091). Metric is CodeXGLUE-style character-level edit similarity and exact match.\", \"cross_file_first denotes the context-ordering variant of cross-file retrieval where cross-file snippets are prepended before the in-file prefix in the prompt.\", \"GPT-2 Small (124M) is the canonical 'small' model arm; GPT-2 medium is a size-parity sensor only.\", \"CodeLlama-7b-Python is the appropriate code-specialized 7B variant.\", \"Mode A (code-as-natural-language concatenation) is the primary paired prompt format applied identically to both arms; Mode B (FIM with PRE/SUF markers) is reported only as a CodeLlama-only arm.\", \"Per-instance paired test is the primary statistical unit; per-repo median reported as sensitivity, not primary.\", \"Python dependencies (transformers, torch, datasets, scipy, ES utility) are not preinstalled in this runtime but assumed installable in a real execution environment.\", \"RepoBench dataset is assumed available as a pre-packaged local copy because the runtime is network-disabled and no artifact was found under /workspace.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Which GPT-2 size variant the brief intends (small/medium/large/XL).\", \"Which CodeLlama-7b variant (base / Python / Instruct) is meant.\", \"Exact semantics of cross_file_first in the supplied RepoBench version: context-ordering, split name, or both.\", \"Primary metric: ES/EM (CodeXGLUE) vs identifier-level F1 vs both.\", \"Target granularity: next-line, next-chunk, or both.\", \"Whether the random split or the hard split is the primary endpoint.\", \"ES tokenization convention: character-level Levenshtein vs token-merge edits.\", \"Truncation rule when context exceeds model window.\", \"Whether to include the FIM (Mode B) contrast at all, and only as a CodeLlama-only arm.\", \"Whether dependency installation and local vendoring of the dataset are in scope for the design document.\", \"Decoding budget policy: greedy-only vs the proposed 0.0/0.2/0.8 temperature sweep.\", \"Sample size is reasonable: 1000 primary, 100 reduced-budget.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-c1655abc-9ec4-4264-bb98-5737b1b27da2", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
